==Evolution==
Evolves into '''HUGE HERMIT CC''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''GOLDEN HUGE HERMIT CC''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
HUGE HERMIT is entirely useless due to a combination of poor stats and weak abilities that completely eliminate its generalist value. Although its DPS seems high on paper, it is greatly hindered by its very low range. It rarely if ever gets to Aliens despite having only one knockback, and even if it does, it's unlikely to do much damage before it gets destroyed. Aliens additionally tend to abuse various abilities, which HUGE HERMIT cannot meaningfully counter. Its long cooldown and high cost are also detrimental, as it can be difficult to replace when destroyed, and tends to be a waste of resources if you get the chance to send another. The chances of it seeing use are few and far between, and it's safe to say even other disposable attackers like [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] are able to outperform it easily.

==='''True Form'''===
GOLDEN HUGE HERMIT CC, despite its newfound abilities and immunities, isn't any more useful. It absolutely does not have the required HP to efficiently tank massive swarms of aggressive Dark threats that deal extreme damage to everything they touch when other specialists like [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza]] already tear through them like paper, while its long recharge time prevents it from keeping up. The same can be said for Warp Immunity, as most Aliens with the ability either do too much damage for it to handle, or can be easily disposed of by accessible units. Combined with its surprisingly high cost, it's safe to say GOLDEN HUGE HERMIT CC just isn't worth the investment. Even when tanking enemies with Warp, units like [[Miter Saw Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Miter Saw Cat]] outclass GOLDEN HUGE HERMIT CC in every way.

